<title>USA: Southwest launches service in Rhode Island.</title>
<headline>Southwest launches service in Rhode Island.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southwest Airlines Co said Monday it launched service at T.F. Green Airport in Rhode Island, its 49th location in the U.S.</p>
<p>The low-cost carrier will offer 14 non-stop flights from Providence to five cities, including Chicago, Tampa and Orlando.</p>
<p>Southwest will add service to its 50th city -- Jacksonville, Fla. -- on January 15.</p>
